From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:20:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: give an SMBIOS type 44 structure the Block Length of
 its data

append_smbios_wine_core_id_regs_arm64 set the processor-specific block's
Block Length to the structure's length minus 6. DSP0134 (Tables 129 and
130) makes a type 44 structure 6 + Y bytes, with a block of Y = 2 + Block
Length bytes: the Block Length counts the processor-specific data alone,
so it is the length minus 8. Every type 44 structure Wine generates on
aarch64 (one per logical processor; on iOS with no ID registers, length
10 and Block Length 4) claimed two bytes more than the structure holds, and
a reader that trusts the Block Length reads past its formatted area into
the string-set terminator. Wine's own reader (wineboot) counts the
registers instead, so it is unaffected. Upstream since 4571d0e869f.

Found checking the RSMB table Red Dead Redemption 2's launcher reads just
before it ends on c0000096 (PLA-401); whether it matters to that launcher
is the phone run's to show.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-rockstar-smbios-conformance.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index 70a653d..087a1c0 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -2146,7 +2146,10 @@ static WORD append_smbios_wine_core_id_regs_arm64( struct smbios_buffer *buf, WO
              core_id_regs->num_regs * sizeof(struct smbios_wine_id_reg_value_arm64);
 
     proc_additional_info->hdr.length = length;
-    proc_additional_info->info_block.length = length - 6;
+    /* The structure is 6 + Y bytes and its block Y is 2 + Block Length: the
+     * Block Length counts the processor-specific data alone (SMBIOS 3.3+). */
+    proc_additional_info->info_block.length =
+        length - offsetof( struct smbios_processor_additional_info, info_block.data );
 
     return append_smbios( buf, &proc_additional_info->hdr, NULL, 0 );
 }
